OF IMPORT DUTY ON CAPITAL GOODS

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE MINISTER OF FINANCE OF THE REPUBLIC OF INDONESIA, Considering
a. that in the framework of national industrial development, the importation of capital goods requires administration that is orderly, transparent, and accountable in order to support the acceleration of investment and the competitiveness of domestic industry;
b. that in connection with the implementation of Law No. 14 of 2028 concerning Customs and Excise as amended by Law No. 9 of 2030, it is necessary to regulate further the administration of import duty on capital goods, including the determination of rates, assessment of the basis of imposition, exemptions, procedures for application, and obligations of importers;
c. that based on considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to stipulate the Regulation of the Minister of Finance concerning administration of import duty on capital goods;

a and letter b, it is necessary to stipulate the Regulation of the Minister of Finance concerning administration of import duty on capital goods; Observing
1. Law No. 14 of 2028 concerning Customs and Excise (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2028 Number 47, Supplement to State Gazette Number 7021);
2. Law No. 6 of 2029 concerning the Amendment to Law No. 14 of 2028 concerning Customs and Excise (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2029 Number 12, Supplement to State Gazette Number 7053);
3. Law No. 21 of 2030 concerning the State Budget of the Republic of Indonesia for Fiscal Year 2031 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2030 Number 158, Supplement to State Gazette Number 7104);

HAS DECIDED:

To stipulate: REGULATION OF THE MINISTER OF FINANCE OF THE REPUBLIC OF INDONESIA NUMBER 169/PMK.04/2031 CONCERNING ADMINISTRATION OF IMPORT DUTY ON CAPITAL GOODS.

