follow the provisions of this Regulation insofar as not otherwise provided in specific legislation.

CHAPTER II
CRITERIA AND AUTHORITY FOR WRITE-OFF Article 3
(1) The write-off of State receivables shall only be carried out against State receivables that meet one or more of the following criteria:
a. the debtor has died and has no heirs or assets that can be liquidated;
b. the legal entity of the debtor has been dissolved and its liquidation yields assets insufficient to cover the State receivables;
c. the State receivables have been verified and it is evident that a minimum of 15% of recovery efforts through legal channels have been exhausted without producing any settlement;
d. the value of the State receivables is insignificant relative to the costs required for continued collection efforts.
(2) Determination of fulfillment of the criteria as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be made on the basis of verified documentation.

Minister after obtaining a written assessment from the committee for assessment of State receivables write-off.

CHAPTER III
PROCEDURE FOR WRITE-OFF Article 6
(1) The working unit managing the State receivables shall compile a complete dossier of the write-off proposal, consisting of:
a. the history of the emergence of the State receivables;
b. the results of verification of the condition of the debtor;
c. records of collection efforts that have been carried out;
d. the latest balance of the State receivables and the calculation of interest or penalties, if any.
(2) The dossier as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be submitted to the committee for assessment of State receivables write-off no later than 30 (thirty) working days after the eligibility of the proposal is determined.

