612/PMK.08/2033

CONCERNING
PROCEDURE FOR GOVERNMENT GUARANTEES

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE MINISTER OF FINANCE OF THE REPUBLIC OF INDONESIA, Considering
a. that in order to support the implementation of national development programs, the Government may issue guarantees over the obligations of state-owned enterprises, regional governments, and other entities financed from the State Budget, thereby requiring a clear and orderly procedure for the granting and administration of government guarantees;
b. that the procedure for government guarantees must be regulated in such a way as to safeguard the interests of the State, ensure prudential risk management of contingent liabilities, and provide legal certainty for guarantee applicants and beneficiaries;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to stipulate a Regulation of the Minister of Finance concerning procedure for government guarantees;

