CONCERNING
ADMINISTRATION OF SHARIA FINANCING

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE MINISTER OF FINANCE OF THE REPUBLIC OF INDONESIA, Considering
a. that in order to enhance governance, transparency, and risk management in the administration of sharia financing, it is necessary to establish uniform procedures and standards for the implementation of sharia financing conducted by government agencies and entities under the supervision of the Ministry of Finance;
b. that the development of sharia financing instruments as part of the national Islamic financial architecture requires orderly administrative arrangements so that the financing activities comply with sharia principles, prudential principles, and the provisions of the state financial legislation;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, and in order to implement the provisions of Law Number 14/2028 and Law Number 27/2029, it is necessary to stipulate a Regulation of the Minister of Finance concerning administration of sharia financing;

the procedures for calculation, payment, reduction, and exemption of the administrative fee shall be regulated by a Decision of the Minister. Article 4
(1) Sharia financing shall only be provided based on a valid sharia contract as referred to in Article 1 number 5 that has been reviewed and approved by the Sharia Supervisory Board.
(2) The sharia contract shall at minimum contain:
a. the identity of the Financier and the Obligor;
b. the type of sharia contract applied;
c. the principal amount, tenor, and profit-sharing or margin mechanism;
d. the obligations and rights of each party;
e. the collateral, if any; and
f. the dispute resolution mechanism, including recourse to sharia arbitration.
(3) Financing officers shall ensure that the execution of the sharia contract complies with the fatwa or opinion issued by the Sharia Supervisory Board.
(4) Any amendment to a sharia contract after its execution shall require a new review by the Sharia Supervisory Board.

as referred to in paragraph (1), the Sharia Financing Entity may apply simplified assessment procedures as determined by the Director General. Article 6
(1) The Sharia Financing Entity shall establish a financing administration system that records, monitors, and reports all sharia financing transactions in a complete, accurate, and timely manner.
(2) The financing administration system shall at minimum contain records of:
a. the identity of the Financier and the Obligor;
b. the type and terms of the sharia contract;
c. the disbursement and repayment schedule;
d. the status of Collateral; and
e. any restructuring, rescheduling, or settlement of the financing.
(3) The financing administration system shall be reviewed periodically and updated to reflect changes in sharia fatwa, prudential standards, and information technology requirements.

system shall be reviewed periodically and updated to reflect changes in sharia fatwa, prudential standards, and information technology requirements. Article 7
(1) The Sharia Financing Entity shall submit a periodic report on the administration of sharia financing to the Director General no later than 60 days after the end of each reporting period.
(2) The periodic report as referred to in paragraph (1) shall contain at minimum:
a. the aggregate amount of sharia financing disbursed, outstanding, and settled;
b. the composition of sharia contracts applied;
c. the status of Collateral and any enforcement measures taken;
d. instances of non-compliance with sharia principles and corrective actions; and
e. the collection status of the administrative fee referred to in Article 3.
(3) In addition to the periodic report, the Sharia Financing Entity shall submit an incident report within 7 (seven) days in the event of material default, loss, or sharia non-compliance.
(4) The Director General may request supplementary information or clarification in respect of any report submitted under this Article.

